Use the graph to convert $6$ kg to pounds.

A currency conversion graph relates Australian dollars ($x$) to Canadian dollars ($y$). Its line passes through the origin and the labelled point $(120,138)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.6]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6.5,0) node[right]{AUD};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,6.5) node[above]{CAD};
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0)--(6,5.52);
\fill (4.8,4.416) circle (2.2pt);
\node[above left] at (4.8,4.416) {$(120,138)$};
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Use the labelled point to find the conversion factor, then use your equation to convert $\$75$ AUD to CAD.
